with the wireframing,

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:45.840
then we had a
strong CI/CD setup.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:51.340
So we are responsible of
the CI/CD setup of the team.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:54.030
So making sure we have--

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.220
so we are using
GitHub, so we have

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:59.250
runners with proper
installations,

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.810
then dependencies, everything.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:05.100
So if you want to do headless
testing for your Shiny apps,

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:10.230
but you make sure that
the proper installation.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:16.260
So setting up with runners
on how to manage the release,

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.190
you know, the
prediction release.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:21.390
So this afternoon
during the conference,

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:26.070
we had the production
release for POS, the 1.0.0,

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:30.760
the first one, which is
like one year of work.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:34.320
So that's quite a
big achievement.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.020
I've also been involved--

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:39.060
so POS is clinical data, right?

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:44.220
I didn't really
give the background,

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:47.040
but when you work in
pharma, pharma companies,

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:50.940
they invest billions
into making a treatment.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.940
It's not just like 10,000,
it's really billions.

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:56.250
So we need to make sure
what you are going to do

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.850
is successful at some point.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:01.980
So you need to analyze
the market on everything.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.620
And this probability
of success tools

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:08.730
provide a data-driven
solution to have

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:14.170
an improved diagnosis for
your probability of success.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:19.220
And finally, I've been
involved in migration.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:22.900
So it's more like in the
server infrastructure.

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:27.280
So to migrate from Shiny
Server Pro to RStudio Connect.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.590
So initially, we
had Shiny Server Pro

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:31.900
and now we have RStudio
Connect so I had

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:34.070
to supervise this migration.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:38.260
So essentially talking
about certain applications

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:43.480
