to validate a piece of software

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.820
or a piece of application.

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:09.290
Not in the code review
and testing sense,

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.970
but in the process
documentation sense.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:14.750
So it was definitely
a learning curve.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:21.470
And we have had a few
iterations of processes that are

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:25.070
based on software validation.

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:30.080
When I say software, you can
think of RStudio, the Shiny

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:33.170
Server, or the rsconnect
as a piece of software

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:41.510
that we have existing, processes
authored by IT to support.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:45.380
But apparently, those
processes are a little--

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.330
there's a little
too much overhead

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:50.070
for a Shiny application.

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:53.490
So, in the past, I would
say, year and a half,

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:57.170
two years we've been
working with our QA

00:19:57.170 --> 00:20:03.020
colleagues, our IT
colleagues, and our colleague

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:06.650
who are managing our deployment
system or analytical system

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:13.100
to communicate both ways.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:16.650
What does quality mean
for our QA colleagues?

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:19.970
What does quality mean for IT?

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:22.190
What does quality
mean for business?

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:25.390
And try to reach
an understanding

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:28.660
of how much testing, how
much documentation is needed.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.920
It's still an ongoing process.

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:37.390
We've had a few pilot projects
deploying apps for use in DMC,

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:44.850
but there are exceptions
for certain studies

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:46.810
that does not apply
to other studies.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:49.590
So the solution
for certain issues

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:53.670
don't really translate
to long term solutions

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:55.710
that you can write
in the process,

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:58.780
in a business process on how to
validate a Shiny application.

00:20:58.780 --> 00:21:01.290
So that's the part
that we're still

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:04.260
trying to figure out
as we incorporate

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:09.670
more different types of
studies in the program.

