Connect is it's a pull.

00:32:48.580 --> 00:32:51.430
So it pulls from--

00:32:51.430 --> 00:32:53.620
it's designed to pull things in.

00:32:53.620 --> 00:32:57.790
Sometimes that's different
from a enterprise scenario

00:32:57.790 --> 00:32:59.590
where they're
expecting everything

00:32:59.590 --> 00:33:04.630
to be packaged up and sent
to the server instead.

00:33:04.630 --> 00:33:07.510
Did you use [INAUDIBLE]
to perhaps address

00:33:07.510 --> 00:33:10.820
some of those
challenges around that?

00:33:10.820 --> 00:33:13.160
Just curious.

00:33:13.160 --> 00:33:13.660
Yeah.

00:33:13.660 --> 00:33:16.652
So, for instance, when
we have like Shiny

00:33:16.652 --> 00:33:21.160
app for instance we want to
send to Posit Connect, so

00:33:21.160 --> 00:33:24.640
first of all, we make
sure it's using renv, right?

00:33:24.640 --> 00:33:27.250
We have frozen dependencies.

00:33:27.250 --> 00:33:29.330
Then we have the CI/CD pipeline.

00:33:29.330 --> 00:33:32.650
We have a specific
section in the YAML file

00:33:32.650 --> 00:33:36.850
which is restoring
packages in the runner.

00:33:36.850 --> 00:33:42.010
And then you have some
instructions to deploy the app

00:33:42.010 --> 00:33:43.510
on Posit Connect.

00:33:43.510 --> 00:33:47.260
So you need to use
the Connect API.

00:33:47.260 --> 00:33:52.600
So you need an API key on
different things in between

00:33:52.600 --> 00:33:55.420
to enter too much into details.

00:33:55.420 --> 00:33:59.830
So Posit Connect
doesn't use renv when

00:33:59.830 --> 00:34:02.980
it restarts the application,
it uses Packrat.

00:34:02.980 --> 00:34:06.370
But if you have frozen
dependencies in the runner,

00:34:06.370 --> 00:34:10.074
it's much, much easier
than if they are packages,

00:34:10.074 --> 00:34:11.949
you don't even know
where they're coming from

00:34:11.949 --> 00:34:14.860
and you try to really
push everything.

00:34:14.860 --> 00:34:17.800
And then you have error
messages everywhere

00:34:17.800 --> 00:34:20.300
in the Posit Connect.

00:34:20.300 --> 00:34:26.350
So from time to time you
see the programs, right,

00:34:26.350 --> 00:34:30.210
but they are
significantly reduced.

